Original commit body from 1fb110c7da9f7cfcd608ab91b599f30ca96aae46:

WI-lipis's third deliverable, the cross-language half. c.yaml filed
fgets/fscanf/fread/getc/fgetc and haskell.yaml filed hGetLine/hGetContents/
hGetChar as fs_read, which is absent from AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, so
`fgets(buf, n, stdin)` and `hGetLine stdin` -- the canonical untrusted-input
calls in both languages -- minted no taint source at all.

THE DIRECTION IS THE OPPOSITE OF GO'S, in the same item. Go's wrapper was
filed ipc_recv, which mints, so a wrong argument INVENTED a source and the fix
removed false positives. Here a wrong argument MISSES one, so this ADDS
findings and is judged as new surface.

MEASURED WITH A LIVE CONTROL PER LANGUAGE, one cold run each, before building:
c's `scanf` reaching a file write returned violated while `fgets(buf, n,
stdin)` with the identical flow shape returned nothing; haskell's
`readProcess` reaching `writeFile` returned violated while `hGetLine stdin`
returned nothing.

WHAT SHIPPED. Both families are now declared under fs_read AND ipc_recv with
boundary_ruling: call_site_undecidable, and `_narrow_by_target_kind` drops the
losing row from the stamped io_target_kind. It NARROWS rather than selects on
every path -- including lookup_with_module's short-name fallback, where c's
fgets actually lands and where the mode seam was once inert -- because it has
to compose with select_by_mode. A `select_by_target_kind` twin was written and
deleted: nothing could call it without breaking that composition, which is
WI-famig's defect (a mechanism with no live consumer), caught by its own
uncovered line.

AN ABSTENTION RESOLVES TO THE FIRST-DECLARED ROW, which is the safety
argument. A parameter, a popen handle, or a collapsed edge whose sites
disagree classifies exactly as before, because fs_read is declared first in
both catalogues. Declaration order is therefore load-bearing and is pinned by
a test against the shipped YAML.

THE CATALOGUE CHANGE ALONE WAS WRONG, and only read-back caught it. fs_read
never becomes a TaintSource, so the surviving ipc_recv row matched fgets BY
NAME at every call site including the file reads io-boundaries had just tagged
fs_read -- one fact with two homes. TaintSource now carries
requires_target_kind, the mirror of the sink side's requires_mode.

Four-way outcome per language, control alive: the stdin read is found, the
control fires, and the fopen/openFile variants stay correctly silent. popen is
deliberately unanswered (its FILE* needs a new io_target_kind -- WI-kanor).

Also fixed, found by the coverage gate rather than by reading the grammar: a
haskell definition WITH parameters is a `function` node, not a `bind`, so
searching only `bind` abstained on every parameterised function -- the common
shape, since a Handle is usually opened from a path the function was handed.

Ratchet 669, delta +0; the c producer half carried one unreachable `return`
that is now restructured.

